-- title:
--   Quadratic polynomial reduction on the Weierstrass curve
-- statement:
--   Let R be any commutative ring and g₂,g₃∈R. In R[X₀,X₁,X₂,X₃], put q=X₂²−4X₁³+g₂X₁+g₃. There exists a function ρ on this polynomial ring such that, for every polynomial p, the degree of ρ(p) in X₂ is at most one and p−ρ(p) lies in the principal ideal generated by q.
--
--   Thus every polynomial has a representative at most linear in the wp-prime coordinate, with the same class modulo the Weierstrass cubic. The result also holds in positive characteristic and for rings with zero divisors. It asserts existence of a reduction function with these properties; uniqueness, linearity of the function, and bounds on degrees in the other variables are not part of the statement.
-- source:
--   Derived quadratic polynomial reduction step for https://prove2.me/theorems/590e44cd-6794-4e85-82c6-06626372866d. Mission context: Senthil Kumar K (2026), Algebraic independence of values of Weierstrass elliptic and zeta functions, Appendix A.2, Theorem A.3 and Proposition A.1; https://doi.org/10.1017/S001309152610145X. This is a derived algebraic tool, not a completion of the zero estimate. Primary Lean sources: Mathlib Algebra/MvPolynomial/Degrees.lean, RingTheory/Ideal/Span.lean and RingTheory/Ideal/Quotient/Defs.lean, revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474. Polynomial induction reduces any polynomial to degree at most one in X2 modulo the Weierstrass cubic. The reduction preserves both the contact-quotient class and all evaluations along the formal Weierstrass curve, so the coefficient obstruction and its bounds are unchanged.

import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Degrees
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Span
import Mathlib.Tactic.Choose
import Mathlib.Tactic.Ring

noncomputable section
open MvPolynomial
open scoped Classical

theorem TranscendenceTheory.weierstrass_quadratic_polynomial_reduction
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (g₂ g₃ : R) :
    let q : MvPolynomial (Fin 4) R :=
      X 2 ^ 2 - C 4 * X 1 ^ 3 + C g₂ * X 1 + C g₃
    ∃ ρ : MvPolynomial (Fin 4) R → MvPolynomial (Fin 4) R, ∀ p,
      (ρ p).degreeOf (2 : Fin 4) ≤ 1 ∧
      p - ρ p ∈ Ideal.span ({q} : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 4) R)) := by sorry
